    "---\n",
    "## Section 1: Macro Copper Demand — The Electrification Supercycle <a name='macro'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Structural Bull Case for Copper\n",
    "\n",
    "Copper is the indispensable metal of the 21st century energy transition. Unlike lithium or cobalt — whose demand profiles are dominated by a single application — copper is ubiquitous across every vector of decarbonisation:\n",
    "\n",
    "**1. Grid Modernisation & Transmission (~35% of copper demand, fastest growing segment)**  \n",
    "The IEA estimates that achieving net-zero requires tripling the global power grid by 2050. Each GW of offshore wind requires ~12,000 kg of copper. AI data centres consume ~20,000 kg of copper per MW of capacity installed. The US alone faces a transmission investment deficit of >$1 trillion.\n",
    "\n",
    "**2. Electric Vehicles (~BEV requires 53kg vs 23kg for ICE)**  \n",
    "Global EV penetration is accelerating toward 40%+ of new car sales by 2030. The Chinese market alone (largest in the world) is already at 40%+ share. Charging infrastructure adds another ~2-4 kg per station.\n",
    "\n",
    "**3. AI Data Centres — The New Demand Driver**  \n",
    "Hyperscaler capex on data centres reached ~$300B globally in 2025, with copper-intensive cooling infrastructure, power distribution, and transformers. Goldman Sachs estimates 160% growth in data centre power demand by 2030.\n",
    "\n",
    "**4. Renewable Energy Capacity Additions**  \n",
    "Solar PV requires 4,500 kg/MW; wind requires 4,000-12,000 kg/MW. Global renewable capacity additions are accelerating to 600+ GW/year.\n",
    "\n",
    "**5. Supply Constraints Are Real and Growing**  \n",
    "- Average ore grade at global copper mines has fallen from ~1.5% in 1990 to ~0.6% today\n",
    "- Most tier-1 projects require 10-15 years from discovery to production  \n",
    "- Resource nationalism (Indonesia, Chile, Peru, DRC) creates regulatory risk for major projects\n",
    "- Water scarcity in Chile/Peru limits brownfield expansion\n",
    "- Goldman Sachs estimates a structural deficit of 8 million tonnes by 2030\n",
    "\n",
    "**The consensus analyst view:** Copper is entering a multi-decade structural bull market driven by demand exceeding mine supply growth by 2026-2027, with prices required to clear at $5.50-7.00/lb to incentivise new greenfield development.\n"
   ]
