    "---\n",
    "## Section 2: Company Overview <a name='overview'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### Freeport-McMoRan Inc. — The Copper Major\n",
    "\n",
    "| Attribute | Detail |\n",
    "|-----------|--------|\n",
    "| **Ticker** | NYSE: FCX |\n",
    "| **HQ** | Phoenix, Arizona, USA |\n",
    "| **CEO** | Kathleen Quirk (since June 2024) |\n",
    "| **Chairman** | Richard C. Adkerson |\n",
    "| **Incorporated** | 1987 (as Freeport-McMoRan Copper & Gold Inc.) |\n",
    "| **Business** | Copper mining, gold & molybdenum by-products |\n",
    "| **Geographies** | USA (Arizona, New Mexico, Colorado), Peru, Chile, Indonesia |\n",
    "| **Key Assets** | Grasberg (Indonesia), Morenci (Arizona), Cerro Verde (Peru) |\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2024 Full-Year Performance Highlights\n",
    "- **Copper production:** 4.2 billion pounds (1.9 million tonnes)\n",
    "- **Gold production:** 1.9 million ounces  \n",
    "- **Molybdenum production:** 80 million pounds\n",
    "- **Revenue:** ~$25.5 billion\n",
    "- **EBITDA:** ~$10 billion\n",
    "- **Operating cash flow:** >$7 billion (35% improvement YoY)\n",
    "- **Unit net cash cost:** $1.56/lb (net of by-product credits)\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Grasberg Incident — September 2025\n",
    "On September 8, 2025, a mud rush incident at the Grasberg Block Cave (GBC) mine in Indonesia temporarily suspended operations. The GBC represents 50% of PTFI's reserves and ~70% of forecast production through 2029. A phased restart commenced in Q2 2026 with return to full rates expected 2027-2029.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Indonesia License Extension — October 2025 (Major Strategic Win)\n",
    "FCX secured a life-of-resource operating rights extension beyond 2041, in exchange for the Indonesian government increasing its PTFI stake to ~63% (up from 51.23%). FCX retains operational control and management rights — a **critical distinction** for investors. This removes the single largest overhang on FCX's long-term NAV.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Innovation: The Leach Technology Initiative\n",
    "FCX's proprietary leach innovation program is targeting 800 million pounds/year of incremental copper production at minimal capital cost by utilising previously uneconomic tailings at US operations. Year 2025 run-rate reached ~300 million lbs incremental. This is potentially **transformational** for FCX's cost curve and production growth.\n"
   ]
